# PncA–PZA Research

This project studies how mutations in *Mycobacterium tuberculosis* PncA relate
to pyrazinamide resistance, using molecular-dynamics simulations and
mutation-level analysis.

The prediction cohort contains 664 mutations: 349 resistant and 315
susceptible. It was assembled by Carter et al. from published mutation
catalogues. Their [paper](https://doi.org/10.1093/jacamr/dlae037) and
[Phil Fowler’s repository](https://github.com/fowler-lab/predict-pyrazinamide-resistance)
describe the source dataset and its preparation.

## Repository guide

- `data/` — mutation labels and derived tables
- `models/` — wild-type and mutant structures
- `simulations/` — topology, NAMD inputs and simulation outputs
- `analysis/` — feature extraction and analysis
- `docs/` — methods, provenance and project notes

See the README in each directory for details, including the simulation
protocol and relevant references.
